[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Objective
[stderr] 
[stderr] Define one semantic input-action vocabulary for web and PWA adapters, covering
[stderr] movement, inspect/interact, confirm, cancel/pause, panels, navigation, and
[stderr] legal combat action/target selection. It makes equivalent actions available
[stderr] across keyboard, pointer, touch, and detected gamepad without creating
[stderr] input-specific rules or committing to unsupported devices.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Dependencies
[stderr] 
[stderr] R0002 supplies shared command/revision safety, R0021 supplies safe session and
[stderr] pause intents, and R0022 supplies semantic controls and focus routing. This
[stderr] contract maps physical input to those existing actions and does not alter game
[stderr] rules, persistence, or shell ownership. GATE-0002 remains an implementation
[stderr] gate for approved browser/device compatibility claims.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Ownership
[stderr] 
[stderr] - `src/platform/web/input/`, `src/app/input/`, and `tests/platform/input/`.
[stderr] - Input binding and availability state plus the semantic input-action API.
[stderr] - Repeat, conflict, disconnect, and fallback handling for supported adapters.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Required behaviour
[stderr] 
[stderr] Use a single action vocabulary: move, inspect/interact, confirm, cancel/pause,
[stderr] open quest, open bag, open settings, navigate previous/next, and choose a
[stderr] legal combat action/target. Equivalent actions invoke the same command and
[stderr] receive the same state/result feedback. A core journey must not require pointer
[stderr] precision, drag, multi-touch, rapid repetition, or a timeout.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Keyboard supports Arrow keys/WASD where appropriate, Tab/Shift+Tab in visual
[stderr] reading order, Enter/Space confirm, Escape cancel/close/pause, and an early
[stderr] Skip to game controls route. Pointer clicks operate the semantic controls;
[stderr] right-click and hover are optional. Touch controls are labelled and reachable,
[stderr] use explicit tap/target confirmation, and do not require pinch, swipe-only
[stderr] navigation, double tap, drag, or long press.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Feature-detect gamepad input rather than promising a model. When detected,
[stderr] pair action text with any glyph; map directional navigation, primary confirm,
[stderr] secondary cancel, and menu pause. A disconnect preserves state and supplies
[stderr] keyboard/mouse/touch alternatives without blocking. Focus-only browser input
[stderr] uses the semantic focus order when presented, but continuous exploration on
[stderr] unapproved targets is not promised. Standard semantic roles, names, states,
[stderr] and labelled alternatives expose the same actions to browser assistive input;
[stderr] voice recognition is neither required nor enabled.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Repeat handling must be action-aware. Navigation/movement repeat is bounded by
[stderr] the shared command contract; confirm, destructive choices, legal combat
[stderr] actions, and target selection accept one deliberate activation per eligible
[stderr] state/revision. Stale, held, or repeated input may not confirm deletion,
[stderr] consume multiple turns, replay rewards, or bypass a modal Cancel default.
[stderr] Surface remap conflicts before saving, while leaving the approved depth of
[stderr] remapping unresolved.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] 
[stderr] The same action vocabulary and adapters apply in responsive web and installed
[stderr] PWA use. Availability may be reported from feature detection, but neither
[stderr] surface promises a controller model or a final browser/device matrix. Native
[stderr] clients, install lifecycle, cache behaviour, and PWA-specific rules are outside
[stderr] this contract.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Non-goals
[stderr] 
[stderr] Do not implement native clients, voice recognition, arbitrary remapping,
[stderr] input-specific gameplay rules, final support guarantees, UI assets, audio,
[stderr] storage drivers, or product gate approval. Do not resolve GATE-0002.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Asset assessment
[stderr] 
[stderr] `asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: input semantics needs no product visual or
[stderr] source asset. Do not create or reserve controller glyphs, icons, illustrations,
[stderr] or other assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Audio assessment
[stderr] 
[stderr] `audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract selects no cue, playback, or
[stderr] mix. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and style version
[stderr] blank/default and create no incidental audio.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Verification
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Use deterministic adapter fixtures to prove keyboard, pointer, touch, and
[stderr]   detected-gamepad events produce equivalent semantic actions and feedback.
[stderr] - Prove held/repeated/stale input cannot duplicate destructive confirmation,
[stderr]   combat selection, rewards, or commands; verify explicit legal-action and
[stderr]   revision checks remain in place.
[stderr] - Prove a gamepad disconnect preserves state and exposes a usable
[stderr]   keyboard/mouse/touch fallback. Compare metadata, provenance, requirements,
[stderr]   dependencies, and ownership to IMP-0023 and the manifest while retaining
[stderr]   GATE-0002.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Evidence
[stderr] 
[stderr] Retain cross-input action traces, repeat-safety and stale-input fixtures,
[stderr] disconnect/fallback output, manifest/catalogue comparison, and the unresolved
[stderr] GATE-0002 record.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Keyboard, pointer, touch, and feature-detected gamepad map to equivalent
[stderr]   semantic actions with labelled accessible fallbacks.
[stderr] - Repeat, stale input, and gamepad disconnect cannot duplicate destructive or
[stderr]   turn actions and leave a usable fallback.
[stderr] - GATE-0002, remapping depth, and unapproved target compatibility remain
[stderr]   explicit and unresolved.
