[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Define settings and accessible-feedback contracts for the shared web/PWA UI:
[stderr] +text, contrast, non-colour state cues, motion, master/music/effects controls,
[stderr] +and caption visibility. They make preference state and its honest persistence
[stderr] +outcome available without selecting storage, audio assets, locales, or an
[stderr] +assistive-technology support matrix.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0010 supplies the accessibility foundation, R0006 supplies independent local
[stderr] +preference recovery, and R0022 supplies settings navigation and focus routing.
[stderr] +This contract consumes their public states. GATE-0002 retains the approved
[stderr] +browser/device/AT matrix, GATE-0003 retains storage policy, and GATE-0004
[stderr] +retains audio, localisation, font, and contrast production choices.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `src/app/settings/`, `src/app/accessibility/`, and `tests/app/accessibility/`.
[stderr] +- Local preference and caption view state, plus settings and accessible-status
[stderr] +  API contracts.
[stderr] +- Preference isolation, failure presentation, and reset-confirmation rules.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Settings are reachable before a new game and while paused. Expose text size,
[stderr] +higher contrast, non-colour state markers, motion reduction, caption
[stderr] +visibility, and master/music/effects controls with visible labels and current
[stderr] +state. Health, enemy intent, quest/save state, and map interactions retain
[stderr] +text equivalents; settings and status changes have concise, deduplicated
[stderr] +accessible feedback rather than animation-frame announcements.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Caption state controls concise speaker and relevant-sound text for every
[stderr] +non-text audio cue that conveys story, instruction, combat state, or warning.
[stderr] +It reserves no cues, assets, timing, language, or mix. Reduced motion lets a
[stderr] +player pause, slow, or disable nonessential movement and screen effects; no
[stderr] +essential dialogue, choice, error, or recovery message times out.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Preferences are separate from campaign saves. On a preference-write failure,
[stderr] +retain the current session choice, say that it will not persist, and keep a
[stderr] +usable default; do not claim persistence succeeded. Reset identifies affected
[stderr] +preference categories, starts with a safe Cancel action, and changes no
[stderr] +campaign, checkpoint, cache, diagnostic, or recovery data.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Responsive web and installed PWA share this preference model, caption state,
[stderr] +and semantic feedback. Storage selection, service workers, cache lifecycle,
[stderr] +installation, update activation, and a compatibility promise remain outside
[stderr] +this contract.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not create audio or visual assets, select locales, choose storage, claim
[stderr] +WCAG conformance or a support matrix, implement cloud preferences, alter
[stderr] +campaign saves, or resolve GATE-0002, GATE-0003, or GATE-0004.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: settings, captions, and feedback rules
[stderr] +create no product asset. `asset_ids` remains blank; do not reserve fonts,
[stderr] +icons, mockups, illustrations, or caption/audio assets.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Audio assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract exposes preference and
[stderr] +caption state but selects no cue, playback, mix, or source audio. Keep audio
[stderr] +metadata blank/default and defer audio scope to GATE-0004.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Verification
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Use deterministic fixtures to prove reduced-motion, text/non-colour state,
[stderr] +  caption visibility, and accessible-status changes preserve semantic labels.
[stderr] +- Prove a failed preference write retains the session choice, reports its
[stderr] +  non-persistence, and cannot affect campaign saves; prove reset starts on
[stderr] +  Cancel and is preference-only.
[stderr] +- Compare metadata, requirements, provenance, dependencies, and ownership to
[stderr] +  IMP-0024 and the manifest while retaining all three gates.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Evidence
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Retain preference-isolation, write-failure, reset-confirmation, caption/motion,
[stderr] +and semantic-status fixtures; manifest/catalogue comparison; and the retained
[stderr] +GATE-0002, GATE-0003, and GATE-0004 records.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Settings isolate accessible preferences from campaign saves and cover motion,
[stderr] +  captions, text, contrast, non-colour feedback, and honest write failure.
[stderr] +- No audio/visual asset, locale, cloud preference, compatibility, or WCAG
[stderr] +  conformance claim is introduced.
[stderr] +- GATE-0002, GATE-0003, and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation gates.
