[stderr] +browser_impact: not_applicable
[stderr] +playwright_spec:
[stderr] +---
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Define focus-safe, recoverable UI states for empty content, invalid actions,
[stderr] +save/recovery failures, destructive choices, and privacy-sensitive diagnostics.
[stderr] +The contract presents supplied session, persistence, and diagnostic outcomes
[stderr] +without introducing transport, cache lifecycle, automatic repair, or support
[stderr] +services.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0006 supplies local recovery semantics, R0009 supplies local-only diagnostic
[stderr] +boundaries, R0021 supplies session/checkpoint presentation, and R0022 supplies
[stderr] +dialogs and focus return. GATE-0003 retains storage/recovery policy and
[stderr] +GATE-0005 retains diagnostics transport and operations policy.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `src/app/recovery/`, `src/app/dialogs/`, and `tests/app/recovery/`.
[stderr] +- Recovery and confirmation view state, plus recoverable-error and
[stderr] +  confirmation API contracts.
[stderr] +- Clear next-action copy, safe dialog defaults, and privacy presentation.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Empty inventory, quest, and save states state what is empty, why it may be,
[stderr] +and the next useful action. Invalid actions, locked exits, and unavailable
[stderr] +targets name the unmet requirement, preserve player/turn state, and return
[stderr] +focus to legal choices; generic error text alone is insufficient.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Save, corruption, and interrupted-write states never claim success before the
[stderr] +confirmed checkpoint supplied by R0021. Retain the last valid checkpoint and
[stderr] +offer only the recovery routes supplied by R0006: retry, return to title, and
[stderr] +fallback/new game. Quarantine messaging explains that data is preserved but
[stderr] +unusable and avoids blame. Fault recovery likewise offers plain-language retry,
[stderr] +title, and safe-recovery choices; a diagnostic option is optional and separate.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Delete-save confirmation names the selected slot and available progress/time,
[stderr] +states irreversibility, starts focus on Cancel, and makes Delete distinct. A
[stderr] +stale or repeated input cannot activate it. Deletion is limited to the selected
[stderr] +local slot and associated recovery metadata. New game explains replacement and
[stderr] +uses a separate slot or explicit replacement confirmation. Settings reset is
[stderr] +preference-only.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +P0 sends no telemetry. Before local diagnostic creation/export, state purpose,
[stderr] +minimal fields, retention, deletion control, and no effect on play. Clear-data
[stderr] +confirmation is local-only; diagnostics UI never exposes save contents or
[stderr] +dialogue.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Web and installed PWA use the same recovery and dialog contract. PWA offline,
[stderr] +install, cache, and update messages only describe supplied status and save-safe
[stderr] +boundaries; no service-worker, cache, update, or remote-support lifecycle is
[stderr] +implemented or promised here.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not select storage policy, send diagnostics, automate destructive repair,
[stderr] +create a cache lifecycle, expose remote support, alter persistence drivers,
[stderr] +make assets, or resolve GATE-0003 or GATE-0005.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: recovery copy and view-state rules create
[stderr] +no product asset. `asset_ids` remains blank; do not create or reserve visual
[stderr] +or source assets.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Audio assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: recovery and confirmation state selects no
[stderr] +cue, playback, mix, or source audio. Keep all audio metadata blank/default.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Verification
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Use fixtures to prove each empty/invalid state gives a legal next action and
[stderr] +  preserves state and focus.
[stderr] +- Prove failed/corrupt/interrupted saves retain the last valid checkpoint and
[stderr] +  offer only legal recovery routes without asserting unconfirmed success.
[stderr] +- Prove destructive dialogs start on Cancel and stale/repeated activation
[stderr] +  cannot delete; prove diagnostic copy stays local/minimised. Compare the
[stderr] +  contract with IMP-0025 and the manifest while retaining both gates.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Evidence
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Retain empty/invalid, checkpoint/recovery, destructive-confirmation,
[stderr] +diagnostic-boundary, focus-return, and manifest/catalogue fixtures, with the
[stderr] +unresolved GATE-0003 and GATE-0005 records.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Empty, invalid, save-failure, and fault states preserve state and expose
[stderr] +  clear legal recovery actions.
[stderr] +- Destructive and diagnostics states are focus-safe, minimised, local-only,
[stderr] +  and cannot use stale/repeated activation to delete data.
[stderr] +- GATE-0003 and GATE-0005 remain explicit implementation gates.
