[stderr] +---
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Define deterministic SHARD-03 integration evidence that cross-checks session,
[stderr] +semantic shell, input adapters, accessible settings, and recoverable UI states.
[stderr] +It produces a traceable evidence matrix and handoff to SHARD-04 without a
[stderr] +real-device certification, browser/device matrix, PWA lifecycle, release
[stderr] +approval, or product asset.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0021–R0025 own the session, shell, input, settings, and recovery contracts.
[stderr] +This runbook only coordinates their public fixtures and must not change their
[stderr] +APIs or duplicate their ownership. GATE-0002 retains compatibility and numeric
[stderr] +release evidence; GATE-0003 retains storage policy; GATE-0004 retains content,
[stderr] +audio, localisation, and visual-production choices. SHARD-04 remains queued
[stderr] +until its separate GATE-0002, GATE-0005, and GATE-0007 handoff conditions.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `tests/app/accessibility-integration/` and `docs/ui-handoff.md`.
[stderr] +- Accessibility/input evidence matrix and documented SHARD-04 handoff.
[stderr] +- Cross-contract fixture composition and provenance review only.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Create deterministic fixtures that cover each SHARD-03 contract exactly once:
[stderr] +R0021 session/checkpoint honesty; R0022 semantic landmarks, panel/focus/reflow;
[stderr] +R0023 keyboard, pointer, touch, gamepad equivalence and repeat safety; R0024
[stderr] +preferences, captions, motion, non-colour cues, and independent failure; and
[stderr] +R0025 recovery, destructive confirmation, and diagnostics minimisation.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The matrix records requirement IDs, source/catalougue provenance, owner,
[stderr] +fixture, expected invariant, evidence location, and retained gate. It checks
[stderr] +visible focus, accurate accessible names, semantic assistive-input operation,
[stderr] +keyboard/touch/mouse/gamepad alternatives, captions, reduced motion, 44 CSS-px
[stderr] +touch-target review, 200% text/reflow review, clear next action, and safe
[stderr] +save/recovery/update boundaries as contract criteria—not as a device or release
[stderr] +certification.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Handoff to SHARD-04 names the evidence it may consume: deterministic
[stderr] +cross-contract fixture traces, gate records, and explicitly unverified
[stderr] +browser/device/performance/release evidence. It must not implement or imply a
[stderr] +service worker, cached-release policy, real-device test result, compatibility
[stderr] +matrix, hosting, certification, or release approval.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The evidence compares shared web/PWA semantic contracts only. Browser/device
[stderr] +coverage, PWA installation, service-worker/cache/update lifecycle,
[stderr] +performance budgets, hosting, and release evidence belong to queued SHARD-04
[stderr] +after its gates; no browser spec is introduced by this documentation contract.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not certify devices, implement product UI/PWA behaviour, create assets or
[stderr] +audio, change prior owners, resolve gates, or advance/allocate SHARD-04.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: the matrix and handoff create no product
[stderr] +asset. `asset_ids` remains blank; do not reserve or create assets.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Audio assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: evidence reviews caption/feedback
[stderr] +contracts but selects no cue, playback, mix, or audio asset. Keep audio
[stderr] +metadata blank/default.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Verification
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Structurally review the matrix to prove R0021–R0025 appear once, with their
[stderr] +  ownership, requirement/provenance links, fixture, invariant, and gate.
[stderr] +- Run deterministic composed fixtures for focus, semantic names, input
[stderr] +  equivalence/repeat safety, preferences, recovery, and destructive defaults.
[stderr] +- Verify the SHARD-04 handoff preserves unverified compatibility/performance/
[stderr] +  release evidence and GATE-0002, GATE-0003, GATE-0004 plus SHARD-04's
[stderr] +  GATE-0005 and GATE-0007; compare metadata to IMP-0026 and the manifest.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Evidence
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Retain the complete SHARD-03 matrix, fixture traces, ownership/provenance
[stderr] +comparison, retained-gate register, and the SHARD-04 handoff record.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Deterministic evidence covers every SHARD-03 session, shell, input,
[stderr] +  settings, and recovery contract exactly once.
[stderr] +- Evidence distinguishes contract checks from unapproved device, performance,
[stderr] +  PWA-lifecycle, and release claims.
[stderr] +- The SHARD-04 handoff and all retained gates remain explicit and unadvanced.
