ected-slot deletion with focus-safe confirmation.\",\n    \"prerequisites\": [\n      \"IMP-0006\",\n      \"IMP-0009\",\n      \"IMP-0021\",\n      \"IMP-0022\"\n    ],\n    \"ownership\": {\n      \"files\": [\n        \"src/app/recovery/\",\n        \"src/app/dialogs/\",\n        \"tests/app/recovery/\"\n      ],\n      \"data\": [\n        \"recovery and confirmation view state\"\n      ],\n      \"api\": [\n        \"recoverable error and confirmation API\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"forbidden_scope\": [\n      \"diagnostic transport\",\n      \"automatic destructive repair\",\n      \"cache lifecycle\",\n      \"remote support\"\n    ],\n    \"verification\": \"Fixtures prove destructive actions start on Cancel, invalid actions preserve state, and recovery exposes legal next actions.\",\n    \"human_external_gate\": \"GATE-0003 and GATE-0005 remain explicit for storage policy and diagnostics transport.\",\n    \"complexity\": \"medium\",\n    \"status\": \"ready_for_authoring\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"IMP-0026\",\n    \"title\": \"Add SHARD-03 accessibility and input integration evidence\",\n    \"domain\": \"tests\",\n    \"targets\": [\n      \"web\",\n      \"pwa\"\n    ],\n    \"requirement_ids\": [\n      \"REQ-0007\",\n      \"REQ-0009\",\n      \"REQ-0010\",\n      \"NFR-0004\"\n    ],\n    \"bounded_outcome\": \"Deterministic contract fixtures cross-check session, shell, input, settings, and recovery boundaries while reserving browser/device matrix evidence for the approved release gate.\",\n    \"prerequisites\": [\n      \"IMP-0021\",\n      \"IMP-0022\",\n      \"IMP-0023\",\n      \"IMP-0024\",\n      \"IMP-0025\"\n    ],\n    \"ownership\": {\n      \"files\": [\n        \"tests/app/accessibility-integration/\",\n        \"docs/ui-handoff.md\"\n      ],\n      \"data\": [\n        \"accessibility and input evidence matrix\"\n      ],\n      \"api\": [\n        \"documented SHARD-04 handoff\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"forbidden_scope\": [\n      \"real-device certification\",\n      \"PWA service worker\",\n      \"product assets\",\n      \"release approval\"\n    ],\n    \"verification\": \"Structural review finds every SHARD-03 contract covered once and preserves all retained gates.\",\n    \"human_external_gate\": \"GATE-0002, GATE-0003, and GATE-0004 remain unresolved.\",\n    \"complexity\": \"medium\",\n    \"status\": \"ready_for_authoring\"\n  }\n]\n81:## Accessibility policy\n94:## Empty, error, recovery, destructive, and privacy-sensitive states\n113:## Content and interaction review checklist\nsed: projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/TEMPLATE.md: No such file or directory\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '76,145p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md; rg --files projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4 | rg '(\"'^|/)(TEMPLATE|F014).*'\"\\\\.md\"'$|authoring-runbooks/B0010'\"\\\\.md\"'$'\"'; sed -n '1,180p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\n| Touch | On-screen controls are reachable, labelled, and may be toggled in settings. Use tap-to-confirm and explicit target selection; do not require pinch, swipe-only navigation, double tap, drag, or long press. A touch action has the same feedback as its keyboard equivalent. |\n| Gamepad | Feature-detect rather than promise a model. Show button glyphs only after detection and accompany them with action text. D-pad/left stick navigates; primary face button confirms; secondary face button cancels; menu button pauses; shoulder buttons may switch top-level panels when discoverable. A disconnected controller preserves state and presents keyboard/mouse/touch alternatives without blocking. |\n| Remote / focus-only devices | These are not a selected delivery target. If a browser presents only directional/confirm/back focus input, the menus use the gamepad-style focus order and all core controls remain reachable; continuous exploration is not promised until a target/device decision is approved. |\n| Voice and other assistive input | Voice command recognition is not collected, enabled, or required in P0. Controls expose standard semantic HTML roles, names, states, and operable buttons so browser voice control, switch control, eye tracking, and other assistive input can target visible actions by label. Canvas/world interactions have equivalent labelled UI prompts and action-list routes. |\n\n## Accessibility policy\n\nThe release target is WCAG 2.2 AA for the public UI and the operable game controls, evaluated with automated checks and manual keyboard, screen-reader, zoom/reflow, touch, and reduced-motion review on the approved browser/device matrix. This is a product quality target; exact assistive-technology combinations remain a release approval gate rather than an invented compatibility claim.\n\n- Use semantic landmarks for banner/title navigation, main game controls, complementary objective/status, and dialogs. Mark decorative art as hidden from assistive technology. Give the world canvas a concise labelled description and provide its essential current state through adjacent semantic status and action elements.\n- Every interactive element has a unique accessible name that matches its visible label where one exists. Examples: `Open quest: Relight the Beacon`, `Use Moss Tonic on Rowan`, `Close inventory`, `Save slot 1`, and `Delete slot 1`.\n- Dialogues announce speaker and text through a controlled, non-interrupting status mechanism; combat announces turn start, selected action/target, damage/healing, and victory/defeat without flooding announcements for decorative animation frames. Notifications are concise, deduplicated, and reviewable in the status/quest panel.\n- Focus is visible at all times, enters a dialog at its heading or first safe action, remains contained only while that blocking dialog is open, and returns to its invoking control when closed. A newly opened non-modal panel receives focus on its heading. Error focus moves to an actionable summary, not an arbitrary visual element.\n- Do not use flicker above three flashes per second. Provide captions/subtitles for all non-text audio that conveys story, instruction, combat state, or warning; identify speaker and relevant sound in concise text. Master audio, music, effects, caption visibility, text size, contrast, and motion settings are reachable before starting a new game and while paused.\n- Required state has a text equivalent: party health uses values and state wording as well as bars; enemy intent uses a label/icon; map interaction, quest progression, and save status use text. Visual settings include a higher-contrast mode and non-colour state markers.\n- Users can pause, slow, or disable nonessential movement and screen effects. No essential dialogue, battle selection, confirmation, error message, or recovery choice disappears by timeout.\n- Settings save independently of campaign saves where storage permits. If persistence fails, keep the in-session choice, state that it will not persist, and preserve a usable default. Reset settings is confirmed and describes the affected preference categories.\n\n## Empty, error, recovery, destructive, and privacy-sensitive states\n\n| Situation | Experience requirement |\n| --- | --- |\n| Empty inventory / no quest / no save | State what is empty, why it may be empty, and the next useful action: e.g., `No items yet\u2014explore the town and finish the first encounter.` No decorative blank panels. |\n| Invalid action, locked exit, unavailable target | Keep the player\u2019s state and turn intact; name the unmet requirement and return focus to the legal choices. Do not use a generic `Error` as the only explanation. |\n| Storage failure, corrupt save, or interrupted save | Never claim a save completed until confirmed. Retain the last valid checkpoint; show retry, return-to-title, and fallback/new-game paths. Quarantined saves are explained as preserved but unusable; recovery text avoids blame. |\n| Offline, install, cache, or update state | Explain whether the current cached version can play, whether an initial download is required, and that an update will wait for a save-safe title/menu boundary. Declining install or update does not block play on a valid cached/current release. |\n| Fault / crash recovery | Present plain-language retry, return to title, and safe-recovery actions. Preserve confirmed progress. A diagnostic option is optional and clearly separate from recovery. |\n| Delete a save | Require a confirmation dialog that names the slot, its progress/time where available, and that deletion is irreversible. Initial focus is `Cancel`; `Delete` is visually and semantically distinct and cannot be activated through a stale/repeated input. Only the selected local slot and associated recovery metadata are removed. |\n| New game over an active slot / reset settings | Explain precisely what will change. New game must use a separate slot or obtain explicit confirmation before replacing a selected slot. Settings reset affects preferences only, not campaign state. |\n| Diagnostics and local data | P0 sends no telemetry. Before any consent-gated local diagnostic record is created or exported, state purpose, included minimal fields, retention, deletion control, and that it does not affect play. `Clear diagnostic data` confirms the local-only effect. Never show save contents or dialogue in diagnostics UI. |\n\n## PWA-specific experience\n\nThe web and installed PWA share the campaign, controls, accessibility settings, semantic UI, and local-save behaviour. Installation is an optional convenience: the title/PWA status area explains availability and has a non-modal fallback when the browser offers no install prompt. Offline status is visible but not alarming. An uncached first visit tells the player that the game cannot begin offline until its assets finish downloading; a known-good installed/cache version continues if an update check fails.\n\nAn update notice appears only at a safe boundary (title or paused menu after a confirmed save) and says whether reloading is needed. It offers `Update now` and `Later`; it never reloads during combat, a save write, a modal choice, or essential dialogue. Cache refresh messaging does not imply that save data was refreshed, deleted, or synchronised.\n\n## Content and interaction review checklist\n\nBefore a content or UI change ships, review it against this contract: original provenance; clear next action and empty/error copy; keyboard, touch, mouse, gamepad, and semantic assistive-input operation; visible focus and accurate accessible names; contrast and non-colour cues; 44 CSS-px touch targets; 200% text/reflow; captions and reduced motion; safe save/update/recovery behaviour; destructive confirmation; and consent/minimisation for any privacy-sensitive interface.\n\n## Open decisions retained for approval\n\n- Exact content quantities, party size, localisation languages, full control-remapping depth, audio scope, and supported browser/device/assistive-technology matrix.\n- The legal, age/parental, regional, and certification policies that may change content warnings or accessibility obligations.\n- Account identity, remote sync, multiplayer, player safety/moderation, live operations, commerce, and analytics. These remain outside the offline P0 experience; no social, payment, reporting, account, or remote-data UI may be designed as committed functionality without approval.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0010.md\n---\ntask_id: R0021\nsequence: 21\ntitle: Define shared session and safe checkpoint presentation model\ndependencies: R0004,R0006,R0017\nrequirement_ids: REQ-0005,REQ-0006,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\nsource_specifications: specification/02-feature-model.md#1-game-shell-session-input-and-responsive-presentation,specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0021\nauthoring_batch: B0009\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No assets; session and checkpoint contract only.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nDefine a framework-neutral shared session model for launch, title, new-or-resume,\nplay, pause, ending, focus loss, and confirmed checkpoint presentation. It\ncoordinates the existing campaign and persistence boundaries without owning a\npersistence driver, platform layout, cache lifecycle, or browser event binding.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nR0004 supplies safe persistence/checkpoint rules, R0006 supplies recovery\nbehaviour, and R0017 supplies campaign progression and completion state. This\ncontract consumes their stable outcomes; it does not change their ownership.\nGATE-0003 remains an implementation gate for storage behaviour and GATE-0004\nremains an implementation gate for concrete campaign assumptions.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- `src/app/session/` and `tests/app/session/`.\n- Session and checkpoint view state, session intents, and safe-boundary API.\n- Translation of confirmed persistence/campaign outcomes into an honest player\n  session state.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nModel the lifecycle as `launching \u2192 title \u2192 new-or-resume \u2192 playing \u2194 paused \u2192\nending \u2192 title`. Expose title actions only when available: without a valid\nsave, Continue and Load are absent or disabled with an explanation while New\ngame remains available. Resume starts only from a validated safe boundary.\n\nPause blocks world and combat advancement. A focus-loss intent safely pauses,\nor first reaches an existing safe state where immediate pause is unsafe, and\nrecords a once-per-session explanation for the presentation layer. Repeated\nfocus-loss, pause, resume, launch, and ending intents are idempotent and may\nnot duplicate rewards, campaign transitions, or save work.\n\nRepresent checkpoint status separately from a request or in-progress save.\nPresent a checkpoint as confirmed only after R0004 reports successful atomic\nconfirmation. Interrupted, failed, corrupt, or quarantined saves preserve the\nlast valid confirmed checkpoint and surface retry, return-to-title, and\nfallback/new-game routes supplied by R0006. The session state must never imply\nthat unconfirmed work, an arbitrary combat moment, or remote data can resume.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nWeb and installed-PWA adapters consume the same session intents and confirmed\ncheckpoint state. Browser visibility hooks, service-worker/cache refresh,\ninstallation prompts, update activation, viewport layout, and storage-driver\nselection are adapter work and remain outside this shared model. An update may\nbe presented only at an existing save-safe title or paused-menu boundary; this\ncontract does not implement that lifecycle.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not implement browser lifecycle listeners, cache refresh, service workers,\nnew save schemas, storage drivers, network services, account/sync, UI layout,\ncontent, assets, audio, or a product gate approval. Do not resolve GATE-0003\nor GATE-0004.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\n`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: session and checkpoint state requires no\nproduct visual or source asset. Do not create or reserve maps, sprites, icons,\nfonts, illustrations, or other assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n\n## Audio assessment\n\n`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract selects no cue or playback\nbehaviour. Keep audio IDs, brief, duration, loop policy, and style version\nblank/default; do not create incidental audio.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Use deterministic state fixtures to prove launch/title/new-or-resume/play/\n  pause/ending transitions and that focus loss cannot advance world or combat\n  state.\n- Prove only a persistence-confirmed checkpoint is presented as confirmed;\n  interrupted, failed, corrupt, and quarantined candidates retain the last\n  valid boundary and expose the supplied recovery routes.\n- Run duplicate focus, pause, resume, and completion intents to prove they do\n  not replay rewards, transitions, or persistence work. Compare metadata,\n  provenance, requirements, dependencies, and ownership to IMP-0021 and the\n  manifest while retaining GATE-0003 and GATE-0004.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRetain state-transition traces, checkpoint-confirmation and recovery fixtures,\nidempotence results, the manifest/catalogue comparison, and both unresolved\ngate records.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Session states cover safe launch, title, new-or-resume, play, pause, ending,\n  and focus-loss behaviour without taking over persistence drivers or layout.\n- A checkpoint is presented as confirmed only after durable confirmation;\n  unconfirmed or invalid saves retain safe recovery routes.\n- GATE-0003 and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation gates.\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"The manifest assigns the three new contracts to settings/accessibility, recovery UI, and SHARD-03 evidence. I confirmed the retained gates and the queued SHARD-04 boundary; I\u2019m now adding only those runbooks.\",\"changed_files\":[],\"test_result\":\"\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"The Codebase Memory architecture request was cancelled by the MCP service; focused repository evidence was used for the non-code runbook files.\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"\",\"browser_log\":\"\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/PROJECT_BRIEF.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/README.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md\"],\"updated_files\":[],\"summary\":\"Focused runbook-contract investigation.\"},\"known_limitations\":[],\"browser_coverage\":\"Not applicable: documentation-only contracts declare no browser behavior or Playwright path.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\napply patch\npatch: completed\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0024.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0025.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0026.md\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0024.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0024.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9498c0843bca9c621ab478f13c29c5e36271b571\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0024.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,115 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0024\n+sequence: 24\n+title: Specify accessible settings, captions, and feedback preferences\n+dependencies: R0010,R0006,R0022\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0007,REQ-0010,NFR-0004,NFR-0005\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0024\n+authoring_batch: B0010\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; captions reserve later audio scope.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define settings and accessible-feedback contracts for the shared web/PWA UI:\n+text, contrast, non-colour state cues, motion, master/music/effects controls,\n+and caption visibility. They make preference state and its honest persistence\n+outcome available without selecting storage, audio assets, locales, or an\n+assistive-technology support matrix.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0010 supplies the accessibility foundation, R0006 supplies independent local\n+preference recovery, and R0022 supplies settings navigation and focus routing.\n+This contract consumes their public states. GATE-0002 retains the approved\n+browser/device/AT matrix, GATE-0003 retains storage policy, and GATE-0004\n+retains audio, localisation, font, and contrast production choices.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/settings/`, `src/app/accessibility/`, and `tests/app/accessibility/`.\n+- Local preference and caption view state, plus settings and accessible-status\n+  API contracts.\n+- Preference isolation, failure presentation, and reset-confirmation rules.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Settings are reachable before a new game and while paused. Expose text size,\n+higher contrast, non-colour state markers, motion reduction, caption\n+visibility, and master/music/effects controls with visible labels and current\n+state. Health, enemy intent, quest/save state, and map interactions retain\n+text equivalents; settings and status changes have concise, deduplicated\n+accessible feedback rather than animation-frame announcements.\n+\n+Caption state controls concise speaker and relevant-sound text for every\n+non-text audio cue that conveys story, instruction, combat state, or warning.\n+It reserves no cues, assets, timing, language, or mix. Reduced motion lets a\n+player pause, slow, or disable nonessential movement and screen effects; no\n+essential dialogue, choice, error, or recovery message times out.\n+\n+Preferences are separate from campaign saves. On a preference-write failure,\n+retain the current session choice, say that it will not persist, and keep a\n+usable default; do not claim persistence succeeded. Reset identifies affected\n+preference categories, starts with a safe Cancel action, and changes no\n+campaign, checkpoint, cache, diagnostic, or recovery data.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Responsive web and installed PWA share this preference model, caption state,\n+and semantic feedback. Storage selection, service workers, cache lifecycle,\n+installation, update activation, and a compatibility promise remain outside\n+this contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not create audio or visual assets, select locales, choose storage, claim\n+WCAG conformance or a support matrix, implement cloud preferences, alter\n+campaign saves, or resolve GATE-0002, GATE-0003, or GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: settings, captions, and feedback rules\n+create no product asset. `asset_ids` remains blank; do not reserve fonts,\n+icons, mockups, illustrations, or caption/audio assets.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract exposes preference and\n+caption state but selects no cue, playback, mix, or source audio. Keep audio\n+metadata blank/default and defer audio scope to GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic fixtures to prove reduced-motion, text/non-colour state,\n+  caption visibility, and accessible-status changes preserve semantic labels.\n+- Prove a failed preference write retains the session choice, reports its\n+  non-persistence, and cannot affect campaign saves; prove reset starts on\n+  Cancel and is preference-only.\n+- Compare metadata, requirements, provenance, dependencies, and ownership to\n+  IMP-0024 and the manifest while retaining all three gates.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain preference-isolation, write-failure, reset-confirmation, caption/motion,\n+and semantic-status fixtures; manifest/catalogue comparison; and the retained\n+GATE-0002, GATE-0003, and GATE-0004 records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Settings isolate accessible preferences from campaign saves and cover motion,\n+  captions, text, contrast, non-colour feedback, and honest write failure.\n+- No audio/visual asset, locale, cloud preference, compatibility, or WCAG\n+  conformance claim is introduced.\n+- GATE-0002, GATE-0003, and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0025.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0025.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ca8605fd4d33cd6617d1bf3aa8c6c7fe6b8d0c50\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0025.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,118 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0025\n+sequence: 25\n+title: Define recoverable empty, error, and destructive UI states\n+dependencies: R0006,R0009,R0021,R0022\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0006,REQ-0012,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0025\n+authoring_batch: B0010\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; recovery copy and state contract only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define focus-safe, recoverable UI states for empty content, invalid actions,\n+save/recovery failures, destructive choices, and privacy-sensitive diagnostics.\n+The contract presents supplied session, persistence, and diagnostic outcomes\n+without introducing transport, cache lifecycle, automatic repair, or support\n+services.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0006 supplies local recovery semantics, R0009 supplies local-only diagnostic\n+boundaries, R0021 supplies session/checkpoint presentation, and R0022 supplies\n+dialogs and focus return. GATE-0003 retains storage/recovery policy and\n+GATE-0005 retains diagnostics transport and operations policy.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/recovery/`, `src/app/dialogs/`, and `tests/app/recovery/`.\n+- Recovery and confirmation view state, plus recoverable-error and\n+  confirmation API contracts.\n+- Clear next-action copy, safe dialog defaults, and privacy presentation.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Empty inventory, quest, and save states state what is empty, why it may be,\n+and the next useful action. Invalid actions, locked exits, and unavailable\n+targets name the unmet requirement, preserve player/turn state, and return\n+focus to legal choices; generic error text alone is insufficient.\n+\n+Save, corruption, and interrupted-write states never claim success before the\n+confirmed checkpoint supplied by R0021. Retain the last valid checkpoint and\n+offer only the recovery routes supplied by R0006: retry, return to title, and\n+fallback/new game. Quarantine messaging explains that data is preserved but\n+unusable and avoids blame. Fault recovery likewise offers plain-language retry,\n+title, and safe-recovery choices; a diagnostic option is optional and separate.\n+\n+Delete-save confirmation names the selected slot and available progress/time,\n+states irreversibility, starts focus on Cancel, and makes Delete distinct. A\n+stale or repeated input cannot activate it. Deletion is limited to the selected\n+local slot and associated recovery metadata. New game explains replacement and\n+uses a separate slot or explicit replacement confirmation. Settings reset is\n+preference-only.\n+\n+P0 sends no telemetry. Before local diagnostic creation/export, state purpose,\n+minimal fields, retention, deletion control, and no effect on play. Clear-data\n+confirmation is local-only; diagnostics UI never exposes save contents or\n+dialogue.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed PWA use the same recovery and dialog contract. PWA offline,\n+install, cache, and update messages only describe supplied status and save-safe\n+boundaries; no service-worker, cache, update, or remote-support lifecycle is\n+implemented or promised here.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not select storage policy, send diagnostics, automate destructive repair,\n+create a cache lifecycle, expose remote support, alter persistence drivers,\n+make assets, or resolve GATE-0003 or GATE-0005.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: recovery copy and view-state rules create\n+no product asset. `asset_ids` remains blank; do not create or reserve visual\n+or source assets.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: recovery and confirmation state selects no\n+cue, playback, mix, or source audio. Keep all audio metadata blank/default.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use fixtures to prove each empty/invalid state gives a legal next action and\n+  preserves state and focus.\n+- Prove failed/corrupt/interrupted saves retain the last valid checkpoint and\n+  offer only legal recovery routes without asserting unconfirmed success.\n+- Prove destructive dialogs start on Cancel and stale/repeated activation\n+  cannot delete; prove diagnostic copy stays local/minimised. Compare the\n+  contract with IMP-0025 and the manifest while retaining both gates.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain empty/invalid, checkpoint/recovery, destructive-confirmation,\n+diagnostic-boundary, focus-return, and manifest/catalogue fixtures, with the\n+unresolved GATE-0003 and GATE-0005 records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Empty, invalid, save-failure, and fault states preserve state and expose\n+  clear legal recovery actions.\n+- Destructive and diagnostics states are focus-safe, minimised, local-only,\n+  and cannot use stale/repeated activation to delete data.\n+- GATE-0003 and GATE-0005 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0026.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0026.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0d02ce13c3bd1411475fdfe3d65dfc0aff3f5eaa\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0026.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0026\n+sequence: 26\n+title: Add SHARD-03 accessibility and input integration evidence\n+dependencies: R0021,R0022,R0023,R0024,R0025\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0007,REQ-0009,REQ-0010,NFR-0004\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#content-and-interaction-review-checklist,specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0026\n+authoring_batch: B0010\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; evidence matrix and SHARD-04 handoff only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define deterministic SHARD-03 integration evidence that cross-checks session,\n+semantic shell, input adapters, accessible settings, and recoverable UI states.\n+It produces a traceable evidence matrix and handoff to SHARD-04 without a\n+real-device certification, browser/device matrix, PWA lifecycle, release\n+approval, or product asset.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0021\u2013R0025 own the session, shell, input, settings, and recovery contracts.\n+This runbook only coordinates their public fixtures and must not change their\n+APIs or duplicate their ownership. GATE-0002 retains compatibility and numeric\n+release evidence; GATE-0003 retains storage policy; GATE-0004 retains content,\n+audio, localisation, and visual-production choices. SHARD-04 remains queued\n+until its separate GATE-0002, GATE-0005, and GATE-0007 handoff conditions.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `tests/app/accessibility-integration/` and `docs/ui-handoff.md`.\n+- Accessibility/input evidence matrix and documented SHARD-04 handoff.\n+- Cross-contract fixture composition and provenance review only.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Create deterministic fixtures that cover each SHARD-03 contract exactly once:\n+R0021 session/checkpoint honesty; R0022 semantic landmarks, panel/focus/reflow;\n+R0023 keyboard, pointer, touch, gamepad equivalence and repeat safety; R0024\n+preferences, captions, motion, non-colour cues, and independent failure; and\n+R0025 recovery, destructive confirmation, and diagnostics minimisation.\n+\n+The matrix records requirement IDs, source/catalougue provenance, owner,\n+fixture, expected invariant, evidence location, and retained gate. It checks\n+visible focus, accurate accessible names, semantic assistive-input operation,\n+keyboard/touch/mouse/gamepad alternatives, captions, reduced motion, 44 CSS-px\n+touch-target review, 200% text/reflow review, clear next action, and safe\n+save/recovery/update boundaries as contract criteria\u2014not as a device or release\n+certification.\n+\n+Handoff to SHARD-04 names the evidence it may consume: deterministic\n+cross-contract fixture traces, gate records, and explicitly unverified\n+browser/device/performance/release evidence. It must not implement or imply a\n+service worker, cached-release policy, real-device test result, compatibility\n+matrix, hosting, certification, or release approval.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The evidence compares shared web/PWA semantic contracts only. Browser/device\n+coverage, PWA installation, service-worker/cache/update lifecycle,\n+performance budgets, hosting, and release evidence belong to queued SHARD-04\n+after its gates; no browser spec is introduced by this documentation contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not certify devices, implement product UI/PWA behaviour, create assets or\n+audio, change prior owners, resolve gates, or advance/allocate SHARD-04.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: the matrix and handoff create no product\n+asset. `asset_ids` remains blank; do not reserve or create assets.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: evidence reviews caption/feedback\n+contracts but selects no cue, playback, mix, or audio asset. Keep audio\n+metadata blank/default.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Structurally review the matrix to prove R0021\u2013R0025 appear once, with their\n+  ownership, requirement/provenance links, fixture, invariant, and gate.\n+- Run deterministic composed fixtures for focus, semantic names, input\n+  equivalence/repeat safety, preferences, recovery, and destructive defaults.\n+- Verify the SHARD-04 handoff preserves unverified compatibility/performance/\n+  release evidence and GATE-0002, GATE-0003, GATE-0004 plus SHARD-04's\n+  GATE-0005 and GATE-0007; compare metadata to IMP-0026 and the manifest.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain the complete SHARD-03 matrix, fixture traces, ownership/provenance\n+comparison, retained-gate register, and the SHARD-04 handoff record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Deterministic evidence covers every SHARD-03 session, shell, input,\n+  settings, and recovery contract exactly once.\n+- Evidence distinguishes contract checks from unapproved device, performance,\n+  PWA-lifecycle, and release claims.\n+- The SHARD-04 handoff and all retained gates remain explicit and unadvanced.\n\nhook: PostToolUse\nhook: PostToolUse Failed\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0024.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0024.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9498c0843bca9c621ab478f13c29c5e36271b571\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0024.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,115 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0024\n+sequence: 24\n+title: Specify accessible settings, captions, and feedback preferences\n+dependencies: R0010,R0006,R0022\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0007,REQ-0010,NFR-0004,NFR-0005\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0024\n+authoring_batch: B0010\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; captions reserve later audio scope.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define settings and accessible-feedback contracts for the shared web/PWA UI:\n+text, contrast, non-colour state cues, motion, master/music/effects controls,\n+and caption visibility. They make preference state and its honest persistence\n+outcome available without selecting storage, audio assets, locales, or an\n+assistive-technology support matrix.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0010 supplies the accessibility foundation, R0006 supplies independent local\n+preference recovery, and R0022 supplies settings navigation and focus routing.\n+This contract consumes their public states. GATE-0002 retains the approved\n+browser/device/AT matrix, GATE-0003 retains storage policy, and GATE-0004\n+retains audio, localisation, font, and contrast production choices.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/settings/`, `src/app/accessibility/`, and `tests/app/accessibility/`.\n+- Local preference and caption view state, plus settings and accessible-status\n+  API contracts.\n+- Preference isolation, failure presentation, and reset-confirmation rules.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Settings are reachable before a new game and while paused. Expose text size,\n+higher contrast, non-colour state markers, motion reduction, caption\n+visibility, and master/music/effects controls with visible labels and current\n+state. Health, enemy intent, quest/save state, and map interactions retain\n+text equivalents; settings and status changes have concise, deduplicated\n+accessible feedback rather than animation-frame announcements.\n+\n+Caption state controls concise speaker and relevant-sound text for every\n+non-text audio cue that conveys story, instruction, combat state, or warning.\n+It reserves no cues, assets, timing, language, or mix. Reduced motion lets a\n+player pause, slow, or disable nonessential movement and screen effects; no\n+essential dialogue, choice, error