-confirmation, caption/motion,\n+and semantic-status fixtures; manifest/catalogue comparison; and the retained\n+GATE-0002, GATE-0003, and GATE-0004 records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Settings isolate accessible preferences from campaign saves and cover motion,\n+  captions, text, contrast, non-colour feedback, and honest write failure.\n+- No audio/visual asset, locale, cloud preference, compatibility, or WCAG\n+  conformance claim is introduced.\n+- GATE-0002, GATE-0003, and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0025.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0025.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ca8605fd4d33cd6617d1bf3aa8c6c7fe6b8d0c50\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0025.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,118 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0025\n+sequence: 25\n+title: Define recoverable empty, error, and destructive UI states\n+dependencies: R0006,R0009,R0021,R0022\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0006,REQ-0012,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0025\n+authoring_batch: B0010\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; recovery copy and state contract only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define focus-safe, recoverable UI states for empty content, invalid actions,\n+save/recovery failures, destructive choices, and privacy-sensitive diagnostics.\n+The contract presents supplied session, persistence, and diagnostic outcomes\n+without introducing transport, cache lifecycle, automatic repair, or support\n+services.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0006 supplies local recovery semantics, R0009 supplies local-only diagnostic\n+boundaries, R0021 supplies session/checkpoint presentation, and R0022 supplies\n+dialogs and focus return. GATE-0003 retains storage/recovery policy and\n+GATE-0005 retains diagnostics transport and operations policy.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/recovery/`, `src/app/dialogs/`, and `tests/app/recovery/`.\n+- Recovery and confirmation view state, plus recoverable-error and\n+  confirmation API contracts.\n+- Clear next-action copy, safe dialog defaults, and privacy presentation.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Empty inventory, quest, and save states state what is empty, why it may be,\n+and the next useful action. Invalid actions, locked exits, and unavailable\n+targets name the unmet requirement, preserve player/turn state, and return\n+focus to legal choices; generic error text alone is insufficient.\n+\n+Save, corruption, and interrupted-write states never claim success before the\n+confirmed checkpoint supplied by R0021. Retain the last valid checkpoint and\n+offer only the recovery routes supplied by R0006: retry, return to title, and\n+fallback/new game. Quarantine messaging explains that data is preserved but\n+unusable and avoids blame. Fault recovery likewise offers plain-language retry,\n+title, and safe-recovery choices; a diagnostic option is optional and separate.\n+\n+Delete-save confirmation names the selected slot and available progress/time,\n+states irreversibility, starts focus on Cancel, and makes Delete distinct. A\n+stale or repeated input cannot activate it. Deletion is limited to the selected\n+local slot and associated recovery metadata. New game explains replacement and\n+uses a separate slot or explicit replacement confirmation. Settings reset is\n+preference-only.\n+\n+P0 sends no telemetry. Before local diagnostic creation/export, state purpose,\n+minimal fields, retention, deletion control, and no effect on play. Clear-data\n+confirmation is local-only; diagnostics UI never exposes save contents or\n+dialogue.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed PWA use the same recovery and dialog contract. PWA offline,\n+install, cache, and update messages only describe supplied status and save-safe\n+boundaries; no service-worker, cache, update, or remote-support lifecycle is\n+implemented or promised here.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not select storage policy, send diagnostics, automate destructive repair,\n+create a cache lifecycle, expose remote support, alter persistence drivers,\n+make assets, or resolve GATE-0003 or GATE-0005.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: recovery copy and view-state rules create\n+no product asset. `asset_ids` remains blank; do not create or reserve visual\n+or source assets.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: recovery and confirmation state selects no\n+cue, playback, mix, or source audio. Keep all audio metadata blank/default.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use fixtures to prove each empty/invalid state gives a legal next action and\n+  preserves state and focus.\n+- Prove failed/corrupt/interrupted saves retain the last valid checkpoint and\n+  offer only legal recovery routes without asserting unconfirmed success.\n+- Prove destructive dialogs start on Cancel and stale/repeated activation\n+  cannot delete; prove diagnostic copy stays local/minimised. Compare the\n+  contract with IMP-0025 and the manifest while retaining both gates.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain empty/invalid, checkpoint/recovery, destructive-confirmation,\n+diagnostic-boundary, focus-return, and manifest/catalogue fixtures, with the\n+unresolved GATE-0003 and GATE-0005 records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Empty, invalid, save-failure, and fault states preserve state and expose\n+  clear legal recovery actions.\n+- Destructive and diagnostics states are focus-safe, minimised, local-only,\n+  and cannot use stale/repeated activation to delete data.\n+- GATE-0003 and GATE-0005 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0026.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0026.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0d02ce13c3bd1411475fdfe3d65dfc0aff3f5eaa\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0026.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0026\n+sequence: 26\n+title: Add SHARD-03 accessibility and input integration evidence\n+dependencies: R0021,R0022,R0023,R0024,R0025\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0007,REQ-0009,REQ-0010,NFR-0004\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#content-and-interaction-review-checklist,specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0026\n+authoring_batch: B0010\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; evidence matrix and SHARD-04 handoff only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define deterministic SHARD-03 integration evidence that cross-checks session,\n+semantic shell, input adapters, accessible settings, and recoverable UI states.\n+It produces a traceable evidence matrix and handoff to SHARD-04 without a\n+real-device certification, browser/device matrix, PWA lifecycle, release\n+approval, or product asset.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0021\u2013R0025 own the session, shell, input, settings, and recovery contracts.\n+This runbook only coordinates their public fixtures and must not change their\n+APIs or duplicate their ownership. GATE-0002 retains compatibility and numeric\n+release evidence; GATE-0003 retains storage policy; GATE-0004 retains content,\n+audio, localisation, and visual-production choices. SHARD-04 remains queued\n+until its separate GATE-0002, GATE-0005, and GATE-0007 handoff conditions.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `tests/app/accessibility-integration/` and `docs/ui-handoff.md`.\n+- Accessibility/input evidence matrix and documented SHARD-04 handoff.\n+- Cross-contract fixture composition and provenance review only.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Create deterministic fixtures that cover each SHARD-03 contract exactly once:\n+R0021 session/checkpoint honesty; R0022 semantic landmarks, panel/focus/reflow;\n+R0023 keyboard, pointer, touch, gamepad equivalence and repeat safety; R0024\n+preferences, captions, motion, non-colour cues, and independent failure; and\n+R0025 recovery, destructive confirmation, and diagnostics minimisation.\n+\n+The matrix records requirement IDs, source/catalougue provenance, owner,\n+fixture, expected invariant, evidence location, and retained gate. It checks\n+visible focus, accurate accessible names, semantic assistive-input operation,\n+keyboard/touch/mouse/gamepad alternatives, captions, reduced motion, 44 CSS-px\n+touch-target review, 200% text/reflow review, clear next action, and safe\n+save/recovery/update boundaries as contract criteria\u2014not as a device or release\n+certification.\n+\n+Handoff to SHARD-04 names the evidence it may consume: deterministic\n+cross-contract fixture traces, gate records, and explicitly unverified\n+browser/device/performance/release evidence. It must not implement or imply a\n+service worker, cached-release policy, real-device test result, compatibility\n+matrix, hosting, certification, or release approval.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The evidence compares shared web/PWA semantic contracts only. Browser/device\n+coverage, PWA installation, service-worker/cache/update lifecycle,\n+performance budgets, hosting, and release evidence belong to queued SHARD-04\n+after its gates; no browser spec is introduced by this documentation contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not certify devices, implement product UI/PWA behaviour, create assets or\n+audio, change prior owners, resolve gates, or advance/allocate SHARD-04.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: the matrix and handoff create no product\n+asset. `asset_ids` remains blank; do not reserve or create assets.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: evidence reviews caption/feedback\n+contracts but selects no cue, playback, mix, or audio asset. Keep audio\n+metadata blank/default.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Structurally review the matrix to prove R0021\u2013R0025 appear once, with their\n+  ownership, requirement/provenance links, fixture, invariant, and gate.\n+- Run deterministic composed fixtures for focus, semantic names, input\n+  equivalence/repeat safety, preferences, recovery, and destructive defaults.\n+- Verify the SHARD-04 handoff preserves unverified compatibility/performance/\n+  release evidence and GATE-0002, GATE-0003, GATE-0004 plus SHARD-04's\n+  GATE-0005 and GATE-0007; compare metadata to IMP-0026 and the manifest.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain the complete SHARD-03 matrix, fixture traces, ownership/provenance\n+comparison, retained-gate register, and the SHARD-04 handoff record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Deterministic evidence covers every SHARD-03 session, shell, input,\n+  settings, and recovery contract exactly once.\n+- Evidence distinguishes contract checks from unapproved device, performance,\n+  PWA-lifecycle, and release claims.\n+- The SHARD-04 handoff and all retained gates remain explicit and unadvanced.\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc 'python3 projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py --wave B0010; git diff --check; git status --short' in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\nRunbook-generation structural quality gate (not product/release evidence)\ncanonical specification chapters: 13\nspecification provenance links: 48\ncatalogue contracts: 26 (IMP-0001, IMP-0002, IMP-0003, IMP-0004, IMP-0005, IMP-0006, IMP-0007, IMP-0008, IMP-0009, IMP-0010, IMP-0011, IMP-0012, IMP-0013, IMP-0014, IMP-0015, IMP-0016, IMP-0017, IMP-0018, IMP-0019, IMP-0020, IMP-0021, IMP-0022, IMP-0023, IMP-0024, IMP-0025, IMP-0026)\nmanifest contracts: 26 (R0001, R0002, R0003, R0004, R0005, R0006, R0007, R0008, R0009, R0010, R0011, R0012, R0013, R0014, R0015, R0016, R0017, R0018, R0019, R0020, R0021, R0022, R0023, R0024, R0025, R0026)\nR files missing: 0\nblocked contracts: 0\nunverified contracts: 0\nunallocated catalogue contracts: 0\nreserved asset IDs: 3 (ASSET-CAMPAIGN-CHARACTERS, ASSET-CAMPAIGN-DUNGEON, ASSET-CAMPAIGN-TOWN)\nbrowser test paths: 0\n M README.md\n m supervisor\n?? projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/\n?? runbooks/.supervisor-children/\n\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0024.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0024.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9498c0843bca9c621ab478f13c29c5e36271b571\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0024.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,115 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0024\n+sequence: 24\n+title: Specify accessible settings, captions, and feedback preferences\n+dependencies: R0010,R0006,R0022\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0007,REQ-0010,NFR-0004,NFR-0005\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0024\n+authoring_batch: B0010\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; captions reserve later audio scope.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define settings and accessible-feedback contracts for the shared web/PWA UI:\n+text, contrast, non-colour state cues, motion, master/music/effects controls,\n+and caption visibility. They make preference state and its honest persistence\n+outcome available without selecting storage, audio assets, locales, or an\n+assistive-technology support matrix.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0010 supplies the accessibility foundation, R0006 supplies independent local\n+preference recovery, and R0022 supplies settings navigation and focus routing.\n+This contract consumes their public states. GATE-0002 retains the approved\n+browser/device/AT matrix, GATE-0003 retains storage policy, and GATE-0004\n+retains audio, localisation, font, and contrast production choices.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/settings/`, `src/app/accessibility/`, and `tests/app/accessibility/`.\n+- Local preference and caption view state, plus settings and accessible-status\n+  API contracts.\n+- Preference isolation, failure presentation, and reset-confirmation rules.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Settings are reachable before a new game and while paused. Expose text size,\n+higher contrast, non-colour state markers, motion reduction, caption\n+visibility, and master/music/effects controls with visible labels and current\n+state. Health, enemy intent, quest/save state, and map interactions retain\n+text equivalents; settings and status changes have concise, deduplicated\n+accessible feedback rather than animation-frame announcements.\n+\n+Caption state controls concise speaker and relevant-sound text for every\n+non-text audio cue that conveys story, instruction, combat state, or warning.\n+It reserves no cues, assets, timing, language, or mix. Reduced motion lets a\n+player pause, slow, or disable nonessential movement and screen effects; no\n+essential dialogue, choice, error, or recovery message times out.\n+\n+Preferences are separate from campaign saves. On a preference-write failure,\n+retain the current session choice, say that it will not persist, and keep a\n+usable default; do not claim persistence succeeded. Reset identifies affected\n+preference categories, starts with a safe Cancel action, and changes no\n+campaign, checkpoint, cache, diagnostic, or recovery data.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Responsive web and installed PWA share this preference model, caption state,\n+and semantic feedback. Storage selection, service workers, cache lifecycle,\n+installation, update activation, and a compatibility promise remain outside\n+this contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not create audio or visual assets, select locales, choose storage, claim\n+WCAG conformance or a support matrix, implement cloud preferences, alter\n+campaign saves, or resolve GATE-0002, GATE-0003, or GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: settings, captions, and feedback rules\n+create no product asset. `asset_ids` remains blank; do not reserve fonts,\n+icons, mockups, illustrations, or caption/audio assets.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract exposes preference and\n+caption state but selects no cue, playback, mix, or source audio. Keep audio\n+metadata blank/default and defer audio scope to GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic fixtures to prove reduced-motion, text/non-colour state,\n+  caption visibility, and accessible-status changes preserve semantic labels.\n+- Prove a failed preference write retains the session choice, reports its\n+  non-persistence, and cannot affect campaign saves; prove reset starts on\n+  Cancel and is preference-only.\n+- Compare metadata, requirements, provenance, dependencies, and ownership to\n+  IMP-0024 and the manifest while retaining all three gates.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain preference-isolation, write-failure, reset-confirmation, caption/motion,\n+and semantic-status fixtures; manifest/catalogue comparison; and the retained\n+GATE-0002, GATE-0003, and GATE-0004 records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Settings isolate accessible preferences from campaign saves and cover motion,\n+  captions, text, contrast, non-colour feedback, and honest write failure.\n+- No audio/visual asset, locale, cloud preference, compatibility, or WCAG\n+  conformance claim is introduced.\n+- GATE-0002, GATE-0003, and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0025.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0025.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ca8605fd4d33cd6617d1bf3aa8c6c7fe6b8d0c50\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0025.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,118 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0025\n+sequence: 25\n+title: Define recoverable empty, error, and destructive UI states\n+dependencies: R0006,R0009,R0021,R0022\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0006,REQ-0012,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0025\n+authoring_batch: B0010\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; recovery copy and state contract only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define focus-safe, recoverable UI states for empty content, invalid actions,\n+save/recovery failures, destructive choices, and privacy-sensitive diagnostics.\n+The contract presents supplied session, persistence, and diagnostic outcomes\n+without introducing transport, cache lifecycle, automatic repair, or support\n+services.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0006 supplies local recovery semantics, R0009 supplies local-only diagnostic\n+boundaries, R0021 supplies session/checkpoint presentation, and R0022 supplies\n+dialogs and focus return. GATE-0003 retains storage/recovery policy and\n+GATE-0005 retains diagnostics transport and operations policy.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/recovery/`, `src/app/dialogs/`, and `tests/app/recovery/`.\n+- Recovery and confirmation view state, plus recoverable-error and\n+  confirmation API contracts.\n+- Clear next-action copy, safe dialog defaults, and privacy presentation.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Empty inventory, quest, and save states state what is empty, why it may be,\n+and the next useful action. Invalid actions, locked exits, and unavailable\n+targets name the unmet requirement, preserve player/turn state, and return\n+focus to legal choices; generic error text alone is insufficient.\n+\n+Save, corruption, and interrupted-write states never claim success before the\n+confirmed checkpoint supplied by R0021. Retain the last valid checkpoint and\n+offer only the recovery routes supplied by R0006: retry, return to title, and\n+fallback/new game. Quarantine messaging explains that data is preserved but\n+unusable and avoids blame. Fault recovery likewise offers plain-language retry,\n+title, and safe-recovery choices; a diagnostic option is optional and separate.\n+\n+Delete-save confirmation names the selected slot and available progress/time,\n+states irreversibility, starts focus on Cancel, and makes Delete distinct. A\n+stale or repeated input cannot activate it. Deletion is limited to the selected\n+local slot and associated recovery metadata. New game explains replacement and\n+uses a separate slot or explicit replacement confirmation. Settings reset is\n+preference-only.\n+\n+P0 sends no telemetry. Before local diagnostic creation/export, state purpose,\n+minimal fields, retention, deletion control, and no effect on play. Clear-data\n+confirmation is local-only; diagnostics UI never exposes save contents or\n+dialogue.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed PWA use the same recovery and dialog contract. PWA offline,\n+install, cache, and update messages only describe supplied status and save-safe\n+boundaries; no service-worker, cache, update, or remote-support lifecycle is\n+implemented or promised here.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not select storage policy, send diagnostics, automate destructive repair,\n+create a cache lifecycle, expose remote support, alter persistence drivers,\n+make assets, or resolve GATE-0003 or GATE-0005.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: recovery copy and view-state rules create\n+no product asset. `asset_ids` remains blank; do not create or reserve visual\n+or source assets.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: recovery and confirmation state selects no\n+cue, playback, mix, or source audio. Keep all audio metadata blank/default.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use fixtures to prove each empty/invalid state gives a legal next action and\n+  preserves state and focus.\n+- Prove failed/corrupt/interrupted saves retain the last valid checkpoint and\n+  offer only legal recovery routes without asserting unconfirmed success.\n+- Prove destructive dialogs start on Cancel and stale/repeated activation\n+  cannot delete; prove diagnostic copy stays local/minimised. Compare the\n+  contract with IMP-0025 and the manifest while retaining both gates.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain empty/invalid, checkpoint/recovery, destructive-confirmation,\n+diagnostic-boundary, focus-return, and manifest/catalogue fixtures, with the\n+unresolved GATE-0003 and GATE-0005 records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Empty, invalid, save-failure, and fault states preserve state and expose\n+  clear legal recovery actions.\n+- Destructive and diagnostics states are focus-safe, minimised, local-only,\n+  and cannot use stale/repeated activation to delete data.\n+- GATE-0003 and GATE-0005 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0026.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0026.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0d02ce13c3bd1411475fdfe3d65dfc0aff3f5eaa\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0026.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0026\n+sequence: 26\n+title: Add SHARD-03 accessibility and input integration evidence\n+dependencies: R0021,R0022,R0023,R0024,R0025\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0007,REQ-0009,REQ-0010,NFR-0004\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#content-and-interaction-review-checklist,specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0026\n+authoring_batch: B0010\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; evidence matrix and SHARD-04 handoff only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define deterministic SHARD-03 integration evidence that cross-checks session,\n+semantic shell, input adapters, accessible settings, and recoverable UI states.\n+It produces a traceable evidence matrix and handoff to SHARD-04 without a\n+real-device certification, browser/device matrix, PWA lifecycle, release\n+approval, or product asset.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0021\u2013R0025 own the session, shell, input, settings, and recovery contracts.\n+This runbook only coordinates their public fixtures and must not change their\n+APIs or duplicate their ownership. GATE-0002 retains compatibility and numeric\n+release evidence; GATE-0003 retains storage policy; GATE-0004 retains content,\n+audio, localisation, and visual-production choices. SHARD-04 remains queued\n+until its separate GATE-0002, GATE-0005, and GATE-0007 handoff conditions.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `tests/app/accessibility-integration/` and `docs/ui-handoff.md`.\n+- Accessibility/input evidence matrix and documented SHARD-04 handoff.\n+- Cross-contract fixture composition and provenance review only.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Create deterministic fixtures that cover each SHARD-03 contract exactly once:\n+R0021 session/checkpoint honesty; R0022 semantic landmarks, panel/focus/reflow;\n+R0023 keyboard, pointer, touch, gamepad equivalence and repeat safety; R0024\n+preferences, captions, motion, non-colour cues, and independent failure; and\n+R0025 recovery, destructive confirmation, and diagnostics minimisation.\n+\n+The matrix records requirement IDs, source/catalougue provenance, owner,\n+fixture, expected invariant, evidence location, and retained gate. It checks\n+visible focus, accurate accessible names, semantic assistive-input operation,\n+keyboard/touch/mouse/gamepad alternatives, captions, reduced motion, 44 CSS-px\n+touch-target review, 200% text/reflow review, clear next action, and safe\n+save/recovery/update boundaries as contract criteria\u2014not as a device or release\n+certification.\n+\n+Handoff to SHARD-04 names the evidence it may consume: deterministic\n+cross-contract fixture traces, gate records, and explicitly unverified\n+browser/device/performance/release evidence. It must not implement or imply a\n+service worker, cached-release policy, real-device test result, compatibility\n+matrix, hosting, certification, or release approval.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The evidence compares shared web/PWA semantic contracts only. Browser/device\n+coverage, PWA installation, service-worker/cache/update lifecycle,\n+performance budgets, hosting, and release evidence belong to queued SHARD-04\n+after its gates; no browser spec is introduced by this documentation contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not certify devices, implement product UI/PWA behaviour, create assets or\n+audio, change prior owners, resolve gates, or advance/allocate SHARD-04.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: the matrix and handoff create no product\n+asset. `asset_ids` remains blank; do not reserve or create assets.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: evidence reviews caption/feedback\n+contracts but selects no cue, playback, mix, or audio asset. Keep audio\n+metadata blank/default.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Structurally review the matrix to prove R0021\u2013R0025 appear once, with their\n+  ownership, requirement/provenance links, fixture, invariant, and gate.\n+- Run deterministic composed fixtures for focus, semantic names, input\n+  equivalence/repeat safety, preferences, recovery, and destructive defaults.\n+- Verify the SHARD-04 handoff preserves unverified compatibility/performance/\n+  release evidence and GATE-0002, GATE-0003, GATE-0004 plus SHARD-04's\n+  GATE-0005 and GATE-0007; compare metadata to IMP-0026 and the manifest.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain the complete SHARD-03 matrix, fixture traces, ownership/provenance\n+comparison, retained-gate register, and the SHARD-04 handoff record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Deterministic evidence covers every SHARD-03 session, shell, input,\n+  settings, and recovery contract exactly once.\n+- Evidence distinguishes contract checks from unapproved device, performance,\n+  PWA-lifecycle, and release claims.\n+- The SHARD-04 handoff and all retained gates remain explicit and unadvanced.\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"Authored R0024\u2013R0026 accessibility, recovery, and SHARD-03 evidence implementation contracts with retained gates and SHARD-04 handoff.\",\"changed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0024.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0025.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0026.md\"],\"test_result\":\"PASS: python3 projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py --wave B0010 (26 contracts, 0 missing R files, 0 structural errors, 0 unverified contracts). PASS: git diff --check.\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"Focused manifest, catalogue, canonical experience specification, and preceding R0021\u2013R0023 contracts inspected. The Codebase Memory architecture request was cancelled by its MCP service, so focused non-code repository inspection was used.\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"Structural validator completed successfully for B0010; diff whitespace validation completed successfully.\",\"browser_log\":\"No browser test run: all three authored contracts declare browser_impact: not_applicable and introduce no browser behavior.\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[{\"criterion\":\"Exactly the three assigned R-series files are authored with their manifest mappings.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Created only R0024.md, R0025.md, and R0026.md. The B0010 structural validator reports all 26 manifest contracts present with no errors.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Each output preserves gates, ownership, provenance, and asset/audio assessment.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Each contract includes manifest-matched front matter, ownership, source provenance, explicit asset/audio assessment, verification/evidence sections, and retained gates; R0026 records the queued SHARD-04 handoff.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Structural validation succeeds without overwriting accepted work.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"validate_runbook_generation.py --wave B0010 exited successfully with 0 missing and 0 unverified contracts; git diff --check passed.\"}],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/PROJECT_BRIEF.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/README.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0021.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0022.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0023.md\"],\"updated_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0024.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0025.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0026.md\"],\"summary\":\"The requested implementation-runbook documentation was added. No README update was needed because this is a bounded authoring-contract addition with no setup, runtime, architecture, or command behavior change.\"},\"known_limitations\":[],\"browser_coverage\":\"Not applicable: this task authors documentation-only contracts; each manifest mapping declares browser_impact: not_applicable and no task-specific Playwright spec is appropriate.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0024.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0024.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9498c0843bca9c621ab478f13c29c5e36271b571\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0024.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,115 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0024\n+sequence: 24\n+title: Specify accessible settings, captions, and feedback preferences\n+dependencies: R0010,R0006,R0022\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0007,REQ-0010,NFR-0004,NFR-0005\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0024\n+authoring_batch: B0010\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; captions reserve later audio scope.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define settings and accessible-feedback contracts for the shared web/PWA UI:\n+text, contrast, non-colour state cues, motion, master/music/effects controls,\n+and caption visibility. They make preference state and its honest persistence\n+outcome available without selecting storage, audio assets, locales, or an\n+assistive-technology support matrix.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0010 supplies the accessibility foundation, R0006 supplies independent local\n+preference recovery, and R0022 supplies settings navigation and focus routing.\n+This contract consumes their public states. GATE-0002 retains the approved\n+browser/device/AT matrix, GATE-0003 retains storage policy, and GATE-0004\n+retains audio, localisation, font, and contrast production choices.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/settings/`, `src/app/accessibility/`, and `tests/app/accessibility/`.\n+- Local preference and caption view state, plus settings and accessible-status\n+  API contracts.\n+- Preference isolation, failure presentation, and reset-confirmation rules.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Settings are reachable before a new game and while paused. Expose text size,\n+higher contrast, non-colour state markers, motion reduction, caption\n+visibility, and master/music/effects controls with visible labels and current\n+state. Health, enemy intent, quest/save state, and map interactions retain\n+text equivalents; settings and status changes have concise, deduplicated\n+accessible feedback rather than animation-frame announcements.\n+\n+Caption state controls concise speaker and relevant-sound text for every\n+non-text audio cue that conveys story, instruction, combat state, or warning.\n+It reserves no cues, assets, timing, language, or mix. Reduced motion lets a\n+player pause, slow, or disable nonessential movement and screen effects; no\n+essential dialogue, choice, error, or recovery message times out.\n+\n+Preferences are separate from campaign saves. On a preference-write failure,\n+retain the current session choice, say that it will not persist, and keep a\n+usable default; do not claim persistence succeeded. Reset identifies affected\n+preference categories, starts with a safe Cancel action, and changes no\n+campaign, checkpoint, cache, diagnostic, or recovery data.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Responsive web and installed PWA share this preference model, caption state,\n+and semantic feedback. Storage selection, service workers, cache lifecycle,\n+installation, update activation, and a compatibility promise remain outside\n+this contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not create audio or visual assets, select locales, choose storage, claim\n+WCAG conformance or a support matrix, implement cloud preferences, alter\n+campaign saves, or resolve GATE-0002, GATE-0003, or GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: settings, captions, and feedback rules\n+create no product asset. `asset_ids` remains blank; do not reserve fonts,\n+icons, mockups, illustrations, or caption/audio assets.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: this contract exposes preference and\n+caption state but selects no cue, playback, mix, or source audio. Keep audio\n+metadata blank/default and defer audio scope to GATE-0004.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use deterministic fixtures to prove reduced-motion, text/non-colour state,\n+  caption visibility, and accessible-status changes preserve semantic labels.\n+- Prove a failed preference write retains the session choice, reports its\n+  non-persistence, and cannot affect campaign saves; prove reset starts on\n+  Cancel and is preference-only.\n+- Compare metadata, requirements, provenance, dependencies, and ownership to\n+  IMP-0024 and the manifest while retaining all three gates.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain preference-isolation, write-failure, reset-confirmation, caption/motion,\n+and semantic-status fixtures; manifest/catalogue comparison; and the retained\n+GATE-0002, GATE-0003, and GATE-0004 records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Settings isolate accessible preferences from campaign saves and cover motion,\n+  captions, text, contrast, non-colour feedback, and honest write failure.\n+- No audio/visual asset, locale, cloud preference, compatibility, or WCAG\n+  conformance claim is introduced.\n+- GATE-0002, GATE-0003, and GATE-0004 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0025.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0025.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ca8605fd4d33cd6617d1bf3aa8c6c7fe6b8d0c50\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0025.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,118 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0025\n+sequence: 25\n+title: Define recoverable empty, error, and destructive UI states\n+dependencies: R0006,R0009,R0021,R0022\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0006,REQ-0012,NFR-0002,NFR-0003\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0025\n+authoring_batch: B0010\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; recovery copy and state contract only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define focus-safe, recoverable UI states for empty content, invalid actions,\n+save/recovery failures, destructive choices, and privacy-sensitive diagnostics.\n+The contract presents supplied session, persistence, and diagnostic outcomes\n+without introducing transport, cache lifecycle, automatic repair, or support\n+services.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0006 supplies local recovery semantics, R0009 supplies local-only diagnostic\n+boundaries, R0021 supplies session/checkpoint presentation, and R0022 supplies\n+dialogs and focus return. GATE-0003 retains storage/recovery policy and\n+GATE-0005 retains diagnostics transport and operations policy.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/app/recovery/`, `src/app/dialogs/`, and `tests/app/recovery/`.\n+- Recovery and confirmation view state, plus recoverable-error and\n+  confirmation API contracts.\n+- Clear next-action copy, safe dialog defaults, and privacy presentation.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Empty inventory, quest, and save states state what is empty, why it may be,\n+and the next useful action. Invalid actions, locked exits, and unavailable\n+targets name the unmet requirement, preserve player/turn state, and return\n+focus to legal choices; generic error text alone is insufficient.\n+\n+Save, corruption, and interrupted-write states never claim success before the\n+confirmed checkpoint supplied by R0021. Retain the last valid checkpoint and\n+offer only the recovery routes supplied by R0006: retry, return to title, and\n+fallback/new game. Quarantine messaging explains that data is preserved but\n+unusable and avoids blame. Fault recovery likewise offers plain-language retry,\n+title, and safe-recovery choices; a diagnostic option is optional and separate.\n+\n+Delete-save confirmation names the selected slot and available progress/time,\n+states irreversibility, starts focus on Cancel, and makes Delete distinct. A\n+stale or repeated input cannot activate it. Deletion is limited to the selected\n+local slot and associated recovery metadata. New game explains replacement and\n+uses a separate slot or explicit replacement confirmation. Settings reset is\n+preference-only.\n+\n+P0 sends no telemetry. Before local diagnostic creation/export, state purpose,\n+minimal fields, retention, deletion control, and no effect on play. Clear-data\n+confirmation is local-only; diagnostics UI never exposes save contents or\n+dialogue.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed PWA use the same recovery and dialog contract. PWA offline,\n+install, cache, and update messages only describe supplied status and save-safe\n+boundaries; no service-worker, cache, update, or remote-support lifecycle is\n+implemented or promised here.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not select storage policy, send diagnostics, automate destructive repair,\n+create a cache lifecycle, expose remote support, alter persistence drivers,\n+make assets, or resolve GATE-0003 or GATE-0005.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: recovery copy and view-state rules create\n+no product asset. `asset_ids` remains blank; do not create or reserve visual\n+or source assets.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: recovery and confirmation state selects no\n+cue, playback, mix, or source audio. Keep all audio metadata blank/default.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Use fixtures to prove each empty/invalid state gives a legal next action and\n+  preserves state and focus.\n+- Prove failed/corrupt/interrupted saves retain the last valid checkpoint and\n+  offer only legal recovery routes without asserting unconfirmed success.\n+- Prove destructive dialogs start on Cancel and stale/repeated activation\n+  cannot delete; prove diagnostic copy stays local/minimised. Compare the\n+  contract with IMP-0025 and the manifest while retaining both gates.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain empty/invalid, checkpoint/recovery, destructive-confirmation,\n+diagnostic-boundary, focus-return, and manifest/catalogue fixtures, with the\n+unresolved GATE-0003 and GATE-0005 records.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Empty, invalid, save-failure, and fault states preserve state and expose\n+  clear legal recovery actions.\n+- Destructive and diagnostics states are focus-safe, minimised, local-only,\n+  and cannot use stale/repeated activation to delete data.\n+- GATE-0003 and GATE-0005 remain explicit implementation gates.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0026.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0026.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..0d02ce13c3bd1411475fdfe3d65dfc0aff3f5eaa\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0026.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0026\n+sequence: 26\n+title: Add SHARD-03 accessibility and input integration evidence\n+dependencies: R0021,R0022,R0023,R0024,R0025\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0007,REQ-0009,REQ-0010,NFR-0004\n+source_specifications: specification/04-experience-contract.md#content-and-interaction-review-checklist,specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0026\n+authoring_batch: B0010\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; evidence matrix and SHARD-04 handoff only.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define deterministic SHARD-03 integration evidence that cross-checks session,\n+semantic shell, input adapters, accessible settings, and recoverable UI states.\n+It produces a traceable evidence matrix and handoff to SHARD-04 without a\n+real-device certification, browser/device matrix, PWA lifecycle, release\n+approval, or product asset.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0021\u2013R0025 own the session, shell, input, settings, and recovery contracts.\n+This runbook only coordinates their public fixtures and must not change their\n+APIs or duplicate their ownership. GATE-0002 retains compatibility and numeric\n+release evidence; GATE-0003 retains storage policy; GATE-0004 retains content,\n+audio, localisation, and visual-production choices. SHARD-04 remains queued\n+until its separate GATE-0002, GATE-0005, and GATE-0007 handoff conditions.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `tests/app/accessibility-integration/` and `docs/ui-handoff.md`.\n+- Accessibility/input evidence matrix and documented SHARD-04 handoff.\n+- Cross-contract fixture composition and provenance review only.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Create deterministic fixtures that cover each SHARD-03 contract exactly once:\n+R0021 session/checkpoint honesty; R0022 semantic landmarks, panel/focus/reflow;\n+R0023 keyboard, pointer, touch, gamepad equivalence and repeat safety; R0024\n+preferences, captions, motion, non-colour cues, and independent failure; and\n+R0025 recovery, destructive confirmation, and diagnostics minimisation.\n+\n+The matrix records requirement IDs, source/catalougue provenance, owner,\n+fixture, expected invariant, evidence location, and retained gate. It checks\n+visible focus, accurate accessible names, semantic assistive-input operation,\n+keyboard/touch/mouse/gamepad alternatives, captions, reduced motion, 44 CSS-px\n+touch-target review, 200% text/reflow review, clear next action, and safe\n+save/recovery/update boundaries as contract criteria\u2014not as a device or release\n+certification.\n+\n+Handoff to SHARD-04 names the evidence it may consume: deterministic\n+cross-contract fixture traces, gate records, and explicitly unverified\n+browser/device/performance/release evidence. It must not implement or imply a\n+service worker, cached-release policy, real-device test result, compatibility\n+matrix, hosting, certification, or release approval.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The evidence compares shared web/PWA semantic contracts only. Browser/device\n+coverage, PWA installation, service-worker/cache/update lifecycle,\n+performance budgets, hosting, and release evidence belong to queued SHARD-04\n+after its gates; no browser spec is introduced by this documentation contract.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not certify devices, implement product UI/PWA behaviour, create assets or\n+audio, change prior owners, resolve gates, or advance/allocate SHARD-04.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: the matrix and handoff create no product\n+asset. `asset_ids` remains blank; do not reserve or create assets.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`: evidence reviews caption/feedback\n+contracts but selects no cue, playback, mix, or audio asset. Keep audio\n+metadata blank/default.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Structurally review the matrix to prove R0021\u2013R0025 appear once, with their\n+  ownership, requirement/provenance links, fixture, invariant, and gate.\n+- Run deterministic composed fixtures for focus, semantic names, input\n+  equivalence/repeat safety, preferences, recovery, and destructive defaults.\n+- Verify the SHARD-04 handoff preserves unverified compatibility/performance/\n+  release evidence and GATE-0002, GATE-0003, GATE-0004 plus SHARD-04's\n+  GATE-0005 and GATE-0007; compare metadata to IMP-0026 and the manifest.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain the complete SHARD-03 matrix, fixture traces, ownership/provenance\n+comparison, retained-gate register, and the SHARD-04 handoff record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Deterministic evidence covers every SHARD-03 session, shell, input,\n+  settings, and recovery contract exactly once.\n+- Evidence distinguishes contract checks from unapproved device, performance,\n+  PWA-lifecycle, and release claims.\n+- The SHARD-04 handoff and all retained gates remain explicit and unadvanced.\n\ntokens used\n48,669\n", "adapter_log": "", "test_log": "Structural validator completed successfully for B0010; diff whitespace validation completed successfully.", "browser_log": "No browser test run: all three authored contracts declare browser_impact: not_applicable and introduce no browser behavior.", "screenshots": []}, "acceptance_results": [{"criterion": "Exactly the three assigned R-series files are authored with their manifest mappings.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "Created only R0024.md, R0025.md, and R0026.md. The B0010 structural validator reports all 26 manifest contracts present with no errors."}, {"criterion": "Each output preserves gates, ownership, provenance, and asset/audio assessment.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "Each contract includes manifest-matched front matter, ownership, source provenance, explicit asset/audio assessment, verification/evidence sections, and retained gates; R0026 records the queued SHARD-04 handoff."}, {"criterion": "Structural validation succeeds without overwriting accepted work.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "validate_runbook_generation.py --wave B0010 exited successfully with 0 missing and 0 unverified contracts; git diff --check passed."}], "documentation": {"reviewed_files": ["projects/mock-fa